# Session handoffs. Ephemeral by design: written to start one fresh session
# with the last one's context, and stale as soon as the next thing lands.
# Ignored so they cannot be committed by accident — twice now, a handoff has
# ended up in a repo's permanent history, where it rots and misleads whoever
# reads it next. Anything inside one that is genuinely durable belongs in
# requirements.md or the README, promoted deliberately.
HANDOFF.md
